{
    "word": "mandrill",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                "word": "mandrill",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1c38459a-06e1-4baa-8550-5400bfe72cbb",
                        "entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mandrills"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                        "entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A primate, Mandrillus sphinx, with a colorful face and rump."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ebbf52d-a4f7-445e-bd9d-a80885f21446",
                                "sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                                "text": "For the Mandrills live in society, and their bands are so powerful in point of numbers, and so crafty in point of management, that they are about as formidable neighbours as could be imagined."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8695a1e1-7aad-4395-9283-8a0849afb755",
                                "sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                                "text": "In both mandrills and drills, males have long muzzles with pronounced maxillary ridges and long tooth rows. Like baboons, mandrills and drills have forelimbs and hindlimbs of nearly equal length."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce3583da-201d-4647-ad36-1f3ed9e3bb2f",
                                "sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                                "text": "Mandrills occur in Gabon, Congo, Rio Muni and in Cameroon, to the south of the Sanaga River."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f39529cd-9bfa-4a28-ac04-e0ed46555935",
                        "source_entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                        "source_sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mandrillus sphinx",
                        "target_lang_word": "mandril",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mandril",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2dc8bf0-c4ee-328d-87fc-e967fbfbddc6",
                                        "entry_id": "7b0555a3-ec12-30c9-9361-49ce50b5569e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "aap Mandrillus sphinx die voorkomt in het westen van Centraal-Afrika"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "primaten"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8907087-4dfa-4d09-8119-3b106ef1e1bf",
                                                "sense_id": "f2dc8bf0-c4ee-328d-87fc-e967fbfbddc6",
                                                "text": "In films kun je zien hoe mooi menselijke en dierlijke genen mengen: de ene mens krijgt een neus van slangenleer, de ander een huid van panterprint en een derde de blauwe wangen van de mandril."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5709dfa-0bdd-4b83-b3b8-b142df944136",
                                                "sense_id": "f2dc8bf0-c4ee-328d-87fc-e967fbfbddc6",
                                                "text": "Zon rijtje achterwerken is even schrikken, maar het doel heiligt hier de middelen, al blijft de veelkleurige bilpartij van een mandril verreweg het onsmakelijkst."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f984c8b-b968-4215-92a0-03be962f3de7",
                                                "sense_id": "f2dc8bf0-c4ee-328d-87fc-e967fbfbddc6",
                                                "text": "Dit is onderwylen zonderling, dat alle de gestaarte Aapen, den Mandril niet uitgezonderd, en ook de Pithekos, spraaktuigen hebben, even als het Rendier, waarvan ik reeds eene korte beschryving gegeeven hebbe aan den Professor Allamand, (…)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08983f2a-9a66-4874-b354-39c4f56931e5",
                        "source_entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                        "source_sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mandrillus sphinx",
                        "target_lang_word": "mandrill",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mandrill",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee2eed44-e6df-3786-8d3e-0d6ab18da0e0",
                                        "entry_id": "1a345c7a-8017-3f4c-b1cf-f039c59bdf28",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Espèce de grand singe africain, de la famille des babouins, dont la face est sillonnée, et chez le mâle rouge et bleue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Primatologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "766ed6cd-89ba-440a-b417-9562c8c0fe81",
                                                "sense_id": "ee2eed44-e6df-3786-8d3e-0d6ab18da0e0",
                                                "text": "Le plus impressionnant de tous les babouins est probablement le mandrill (Mandrillus sphinx) de l’Afrique occidentale. Il est plus localisé dans les forêts que la plupart des autres espèces et vit en petit groupe de six jusqu’à une douzaine. Il est omnivore et très habile à attraper les oiseaux et les petits mammifères."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36e94a5c-c517-403f-a764-6d51567488cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "fca3530a-9ece-36dc-ac79-5a5a445c3194",
                        "source_sense_id": "04029319-eaf5-396f-8ed5-b7ff3b0365a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mandrillus sphinx",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mandrill",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mandrill",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acd1368d-c17f-3415-89d9-7b45f8894022",
                                        "entry_id": "c24a3a21-7f83-3711-8e27-5874e4a9ac92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Primatenart mit auffälligen rot-blauen Farbpartien im Gesicht und am Gesäß, die in Zentralafrika beheimatet ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3353e575-5189-4f97-a9a3-4ea05ec18844",
                                                "sense_id": "acd1368d-c17f-3415-89d9-7b45f8894022",
                                                "text": "„Und der Wirt hatte blaue Backen wie ein Mandrill, halb blaurot vom Wein, halb blauschwarz von der ungezähmten Dichte seines Bartwuchses, dem das Rasiermesser nur stundenweise etwas menschlichere Manieren beibringen konnte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17624239-2b0a-4d5e-8402-d84484c4f17f",
